Wasiak Takes Over From His Old Manager
Stan Wasiak arrived in El Paso today to take the managerial reins of the Sun Dodgers from Andy Cohen who took
them from Monty Basgall after Tuesday night’s game with the Alexandria Aces at Dudley Field.
Andy, losing a chance to become the only undefeated Texas League manager of the season and maybe in history,
when: the Sun Dodgers bowed to Alexandria last night 5-1, looked forward to working with one of his proteges this season.
Wasiak. coming here from Daytona Beach, played for Andy back in the early 1940s when Andy managed the Dayton, O., club in the
Mid-Atlantic League.
“HE WAS a hustling third baseman and a_ good all-around ball player,” said Andy. “I'm sure he'll do a good job
here and the fans and players will like him.”
Andy is expecting to continue as coach of the Sun Dodgers. In fact, he has just agreed to make his first road trip with
the team, starting Saturday. So far this season he’s coached only at home.
Several years ago, he was a one-night manager of the Philadelphia Phils. They beat Milwaukee that night. So Andy
has the distinction of being the only undefeated manager in big league baseball.
IT LOOKED LIKE he would obtain that distinction in the Texas League last night. Rick
Rhoden looked like he was going to mow down the Aces. 
He fanned three men in two innings. But he ran intosome difficulty in the third and a lot of it in the fourth. Domingo
Luna and Dave Allen came in to pitch scoreless ball but it was too late. The Sun Dodgers couldn't get to Willie Boynton 
of the Aces except for one run and that came in the eighth.
“Some of Alexandria's hits were off well-pitched balls,’’ Andy said, “and it did look like Rhoden lost some of his
stuff after such a fine start.”
“QUR PLAYERS had tough luck in hitting. They rapped the ball pretty solid but right at somebody most of the time.”
Pinch hitter Bob Long walked, took third on Jerry Royster’s double and scored on Bob Cummings’ sacrifice fly for the only Sun Dodger run.
Burney Beckman, Dutchborn lefty, may face Dave Freisleben of German extraction in tonight’s game.


