Executive Director, Goodwill Industries of El] Paso, Inc.

Dr. Ortego Leaves UTEP
EDITOR: As the purpose of any newspaper is to inform Its readers on a wide range of matters, I think it only proper to
notify those E] Pasoans who do not yet know of Dr. Philip D. Ortego’s departure from the U.T. El Paso campus.
Dr, Ortego, former English assistant professor and director of the Chicano Affairs Program, left the university faculty on
August 30 as a protest resignation. From speaking with him, I found that his reasons were varied. However, what seemed to be
foremost in his mind was that of the 27 high-level vacancies which could have been at least partially filled by Chicanos,
only one Mexican-American was appointed and that, 1 might add, was on an ad interim basis. Fortunately, the temporary
status was changed to a permanent one when Dr. Norma Hernandez was assigned as chairman of the Curriculum and In-
struction Department on September 1.

